ly meets the 'kitchen' purpose requirement. However, the item is described only as a 'KITCHEN TUBE' with no material stated, so it is NOT established that it is glassware (tubes come in plastic, rubber, metal, glass). Because the essential requirement 'must be glassware' is NO CONCLUSIVE EVIDENCE, category fit cannot be established. Furthermore, this is effectively a residual 'other' category requiring every exclusion to be DEFINITELY DOES NOT APPLY; multiple exclusions (notably the glass tubes/envelopes exclusion 7011, and the material-dependent ones) cannot be definitively ruled out given the unknown material. With category fit and several requirements/exclusions unsettled, the result is INSUFFICIENT_INFORMATION.", "status_reason": "Must be glassware - the item is a 'KITCHEN TUBE' with no material stated; a tube may be of plastic, rubber, metal, or glass, and nothing here establishes it is glass", "status_reason_kind": "unclear"}}}, "subheading_evaluation": {"evaluated": [], "matched": [], "evaluations": {}}}, "data_sources": {"web_enrichment": null, "rules": [{"rule_id": 35, "rule_text": "For the purposes of Chapters 74 to 76 and Chapters 78 to 81, the expression 'profiles' means rolled, drawn, extruded, forged or shaped products, in coils or not, having a uniform cross section along their whole length, which do not conform to any of the definitions of bars, wire, plates, sheets, strip, foil or tubes. The expression also includes cast or sintered products of the same forms which have been subsequently worked after production (otherwise than by simple trimming or deburring), provi", "rule_type": {"id": 1, "name": "section notes"}, "scope": {"code": "XV", "id": 14704}, "score": 1.0}, {"rule_id": 38, "rule_text": "For the purposes of Chapters 74 to 76 and Chapters 78 to 81, the expression 'tubes and pipes' means hollow products, coiled or not, of uniform cross-section with only one enclosed void throughout their length in the shape of circles, ovals, rectangles (including squares), equilateral triangles or regular convex polygons, and with a uniform wall thickness. Products with a cross-section of a rectangle (including square), equilateral triangle or regular convex polygon, which may be rounded at the c", "rule_type": {"id": 1, "name": "section notes"}, "scope": {"code": "XV", "id": 14704}, "score": 1.0}, {"rule_id": 672, "rule_text": "This Chapter does not include: Items of glass of heading/subheading 70.11; [References: heading 70.11 – Glass envelopes (including bulbs and tubes), open, and glass parts thereof, without fittings, for electric lamps and light sources, cathoderay tubes or the like.]", "rule_type": {"id": 2, "name": "chapter notes"}, "scope": {"code": "8500000000", "id": 8901}, "score": 1.0}, {"rule_id": 1266, "rule_text": "This Chapter refers only to ceramic products which have been fired after shaping: Headings/subheadings 69.04 to 69.14 refer only to such products that are not classified in headings/subheadings 69.01 to 69.03; [References: heading 69.04 – Ceramic building bricks, flooring blocks, support or filler tiles and the like.; heading 69.14 – Other ceramic articles.; heading 69.01 – Bricks, blocks, tiles and other ceramic goods of siliceous fossil meals (for example, kieselguhr, tripolite or diatomite) o", "rule_type": {"id": 2, "name": "chapter notes"}, "scope": {"code": "6900000000", "id": 10673}, "score": 1.0}, {"rule_id": 913, "rule_text": "For the purposes of heading/subheading 19.01: The terms 'flour' and 'kibber' mean: Flour, groats and powder, of vegetable origin, in any Chapter, except flour, groats or powder, of dried vegetables (heading/subheading 07.12), of potatoes (heading/subheading 11.05), or of dried leguminous vegetables (heading/subheading 11.06). [References: heading 07.12 – Dried vegetables, whole, cut, sliced, broken or in powder, but not further prepared.; heading 11.05 – Flour, meal, powder, flakes, granules and", "rule_type": {"id": 2, "name": "chapter notes"}, "scope": {"code": "1900000000", "id": 24881}, "score": 0.7184646725654602}, {"rule_id": 1250, "rule_text": "Heading/subheading 07.12 includes all dried vegetables, of the kinds included in headings/subheadings 07.01 through 07.11, except flour, meal and powder of dried leguminous vegetables of heading/subheading 07.13 (heading/subheading 11.06). [References: heading 07.01 – Potatoes, fresh or chilled.; heading 07.11 – Vegetables provisionally preserved, but unsuitable in that state for immediate consumption.; heading 07.13 – Dried leguminous vegetables, shelled, whether or not skinned or split.; headi", "rule_type": {"id": 2, "name": "chapter notes"}, "scope": {"code": "0700000000", "id": 6118}, "score": 0.7184646725654602}, {"rule_id": 19, "rule_text": "In the entire Supplement, the expression 'parts for general use' means goods of headings/subheadings 73.07, 73.12, 73.15, 73.17 or 73.18 and similar articles of other base metal; excluding articles specially designed for use solely in implants in medical science, surgery, dentistry or veterinary medicine (heading/subheading 90.21); [References: heading 73.07 – Tube or pipe fittings (for example, couplings, elbows, sleeves), of iron or steel.; heading 73.12 – Stranded wire, ropes, cables, plaited", "rule_type": {"id": 1, "name": "section notes"}, "scope": {"code": "XV", "id": 14704}, "score": 0.6661056280136108}], "guidelines": [{"guideline_id": 146, "guideline_number": "025/88", "title": "39.17 Tubes, pipes and hoses", "text": "39.17 Tubes, pipes and hoses. The expression "lay-flat tubing" in Note 8 to this Chapter means - tubes and pipes as defined in the preamble to this Note, i.e., of a kind normally used for conveying, conducting or distributing gases or liquids and imported in a flat form. Therefore, sleeves of plastic material (which are not sausage casings) and are not for the conveyance, conduction or distribution of gases or liquids, shall not be classified under heading 39.17, but rather as sheets, strips, et", "score":